<?phem

namespace App\Ui\Demos;

use Phem\Attribute\Page;
use Phem\{Event, Node};
use Phem\Ui\Base\Examples\{FormHeroDemo, FormMapFormDemo};

use function App\Ui\{DemoPage, Example, Examples, Hero};

#[Page('/components/form')]
function FormPage(): Node
{
    return (
        <DemoPage slug="form">
            <Hero source="FormHeroDemo">
                <Hero.description>
                    <p>The <code>onSubmit</code> handler of a <code>Form</code> runs on the server, as a Server Function. The browser does not send the form: the submit is an event of the page, and the handler gets it as its <code>Event $e</code> argument.</p>
                    <p><code>$e-&gt;form</code> has the values of the form as an array. The key is the <code>name</code> of each control. The value is a string, or a list of strings when many controls have the same name. Read a value with a default, as in <code>$e-&gt;form['username'] ?? ''</code>.</p>
                    <p>The handler sets the state of the component, and its errors show in the <code>FieldError</code> of each field. While the request runs, phem locks the submit button with <code>aria-disabled="true"</code>. To get the values as a typed object, see <a href="#validate-with-mapform" className="underline">Validate with #[MapForm]</a>.</p>
                </Hero.description>
                <FormHeroDemo />
            </Hero>
            <Examples>
                <Example title="Validate with #[MapForm]" source="FormMapFormDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Add <code>#[MapForm]</code> to a parameter of the handler to get the values of the form as an object. The Validator checks its <code>#[Assert]</code> constraints before the handler runs, and the errors go to the <code>Validation</code> property of the component.</p>
                        <p>Show the error of each field with <code>validation.error()</code> in its <code>FieldError</code>. The field of an error is the property path of the object, so name each control as its property.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <FormMapFormDemo />
                </Example>
            </Examples>
        </DemoPage>
    );
}
